A||||12||sqoach||alright! making progress (sub box)||||10||
Z||000000||sqoach||03-07-2001||02:57 PM||||ok, actually making some progress on my box. i was trying to make it completely out of fiberboard, but it was a pain in the a$$. so, i just have the front and the left side (where the speaker is going to be mounted) out of fiberboard. the rest is going to be fiberglass. but, i'm going to fiberglass the inside of the box instead of the outside. reason is because it's already a tight fit, and i'm afraid if i 'glass the outside, it won't fit.<P>here's a pic of it as of now:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/subbox1.JPG"> <P>now i just need to figure out how much fiberglass i need. how much did you other guys use? i think 2 layers should be enough.<P><P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||10
Z||000001||stimpy||03-07-2001||03:46 PM||||You'll only need the fiberglass to make it airtight. The fiberboard is rigid, so you won't need it to hold the shape like I did with mine. Maybe you may even be able to get away with just caulking the inside. That way you can avoid the fiberglass thing altogether. I'd caulk it even if I was going to use the glass. <BR>BTW, so you're going to have the speaker fire at the console? Interesting. Can't wait to hear it. Remember May 20th! <P>OK, looked at it again and figured out that the back and bottom are posterboard(?) Yeah, glass it up. Also, run some nails through those boards, a good sub and enough watts will tear that tape like wet toilet paper after a while.<BR>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 03-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||sqoach||03-07-2001||06:42 PM||||yeah, the rest of it is poster-type board. it's actually the thin cardboard from a shoe box. i used 4 screws to hold the 2 pieces of fiberboard together, and i'm going to caulk the inside to make sure it's sealed off good. then fiberglass the inside. and i'm going to put carpet all around the box so it doesn't rattle on the bottom of the dash. hope i have enough room for that.<P>i already tried my sub in the box how it is and it sucked. that sub was hittin so hard it about ripped the cardboard. and it was rattling like hell. pretty neat to see it actually hittin though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>i'm hoping my idea of having it fire toward the console works. it's at least an inch from it, i think. you know that little part that dips in to the side? that's where the sub is. so it has some room to move. if it doesn't work, i guess i'll try something else.||||reg||10
Z||000003||stsmithgt||03-08-2001||10:58 AM||||That looks like you used MDF board(medium density fiber).  HDF has smaller particles (High Density Fiber)for a more solid construction.  When your done with that one, sell it and what you've learned during the construction of that one can only improve the next one you build. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I envy you guys that get to play with stuff like that.  I'm still trying to get mine mechanically sound.  Well some cosmetics.  I was trying to glue the glove box door back together that was coming apart.  What would you use if you didn't have the proper equipment?  Everything I could dig up. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Scary huh?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gloveboxdoor.jpg"> ||||reg||3
Z||000004||Standard||03-08-2001||12:42 PM||||Hehe, I love the fork just kinda stuck in there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sqoach, it's looking good!  My progress has kinda stalled, been working too much.  I'll get it done eventually...||||reg||
Z||000005||sqoach||03-14-2001||12:05 AM||||just got the fiberglass done today! i used that fiberglass repair kit that stimpy mentioned to use in his footwell sub thread. then i had to get some more resin. so i got the no-drip jelly kind. that stuff works good.<BR>oh yeah, i also made the inside of it smaller cuz there was at least a cubed foot of air space. now it's around 2/3 cubed foot. i hope this works. i'm planning on carpeting it tomorrow and hooking it up! provided that it doesn't fall apart when i test it out first  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>then i'll get some pics cuz everyone loves pics  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
